<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Universal Links for the canonical customer queue-join QR.

	  The canonical QR encodes https://<host>/join?centerId=... . When the
	  phone camera opens that URL, iOS checks the associated domains declared
	  here and opens QueueFlow when the domain publishes a matching
	  apple-app-site-association file. Without the app installed, or if the
	  domain is not verified, iOS opens Safari on the same URL, which is the
	  Customer Web /join page. That fallback is the whole point of using HTTPS.

	  REQUIREMENTS — these cannot be satisfied from the repository alone and
	  must be completed outside the codebase before automatic app opening works:
	    1. This file must be referenced by the Runner target via
	       CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS, and the provisioning profile must have the
	       Associated Domains capability enabled.
	    2. The domain must serve, at its root:
	         /.well-known/apple-app-site-association
	       (or /apple-app-site-association), as application/json, with no
	       redirect, containing the app's Team ID and bundle ID:
	         { "applinks": { "details": [
	             { "appID": "<TEAMID>.<BUNDLEID>",
	               "components": [ { "/": "/join", "*": "*" } ] } ] } }
	    3. The domain must be served over HTTPS with a publicly trusted
	       certificate. A raw IP or a self-signed certificate cannot verify.
	    4. The domain owner must submit the domain to Apple's CDN; propagation
	       can take up to ~24 hours.

	  Until steps 1-4 are done, the linked QR opens Customer Web in Safari.
	  That is correct, expected behaviour and not a defect.

	  The host below must match the domain serving the file AND the value of
	  VITE_CUSTOMER_WEB_URL used to generate the QR codes, otherwise the QR
	  will not point at this associated domain.

	  The default below is the reserved .invalid TLD (RFC 2606), which can never
	  resolve. An unconfigured build therefore cannot be mistaken for a working
	  Universal Link: iOS cannot verify a domain that does not exist, so the QR
	  opens Customer Web in Safari. Replace it with the real host before
	  shipping, together with VITE_CUSTOMER_WEB_URL and
	  --dart-define=QUEUEFLOW_JOIN_HOSTS.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:join.invalid</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
